#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD1011 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "Generator-wildcard rule: expansion is COLUMN-DRIVEN, so the column list is load-bearing and deliberately minimal - AVISITN is the ONLY name here matching `*N`/`*C`, and it is not in _wildcardExclude, so there is EXACTLY ONE expansion (root AVISIT, with AVISITC synthesised as an absent column). Any extra column ending in N or C would silently add an expansion and change the count. Scope.Data_Structures is [ALL], so no structure= is needed. Row 1 populates the secondary AVISITN while the primary AVISIT is empty -> fires; row 2 has both -> silent. One expansion x one firing row -> 1 violation."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 AVISITN=1
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AVISIT  type=Char
col AVISITN type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 |       | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | WEEK2 | 2
